 Dolby Vision level 1 max_pq (frame metadata @code{lavfi.dovi.l1_max_pq} or
-DOVI side data) when present, else static side data; no dynamic peak
-detection.
+DOVI side data) when present, dynamic peak detection when @option{peak_detect}
+is enabled, else static side data.
 It also accepts a Dolby Vision profile 5 base layer (full range P010,
 colorspace @code{ipt-c2}) directly and applies the RPU reshape in the kernel.
 
+@item peak_detect
+Measure the signal peak dynamically from each frame on the GPU. Supported only
+with @code{tonemap=bt2408_hable}; other curves use their own average peak
+detection logic and ignore this option. For @code{bt2408_hable}, the peak order
+of precedence per frame is: @option{peak} option if non-zero, Dolby Vision level 1
+metadata if present, dynamic peak detection, and finally static side data.
+Default is 0 (disabled).
+
 @item param
 Tune the tone mapping algorithm. same as param option in @ref{tonemap}.
 
@@ -28683,6 +28691,10 @@ The tonemapping algorithm parameters is fine-tuned per each scene. And a thresho
 is used to detect whether the scene has changed or not. If the distance between
 the current frame average brightness and the current running average exceeds
 a threshold value, we would re-calculate scene average and peak brightness.
+For @code{bt2408_hable} with @option{peak_detect}, it sets the scene change
+window: changes below @code{5 * threshold} percent are smoothed, changes above
+@code{15 * threshold} percent reset smoothing to the new frame, and changes in
+between blend the two. 0 disables scene change detection.
 The default value is 0.2.
 
 @item format
